Subject: [PATCH] input: Ayaneo keycodes (AYA_HOME, AYA_SPACE, AYA_CONTROL_LC/RC, AYA_PERFORMANCE_*)

Same labels and values as the stock Ayaneo Pocket DS framework, so the stock
gpio-keys.kl can be used and the Ayaneo apps receive the codes they expect.

--- a/libs/input/InputEventLabels.cpp
+++ b/libs/input/InputEventLabels.cpp
@@ -374,6 +374,19 @@
     DEFINE_KEYCODE(CONTEXTUAL_SEARCH), \
     DEFINE_KEYCODE(CONTEXTUAL_INSERT)
 
+// Ayaneo Pocket DS: keycodes of the stock Ayaneo framework (same labels and values),
+// used by the stock gpio-keys.kl and expected by the Ayaneo apps (AYAHome / AYAWindow
+// key detectors). Name -> value only: they are far above AKEYCODE_MAX, so they are not
+// part of KEY_NAMES, which is indexed by keycode.
+#define AYANEO_KEYCODES_SEQUENCE \
+    { "AYA_CONTROL_LC", 751 }, \
+    { "AYA_CONTROL_RC", 752 }, \
+    { "AYA_SPACE", 753 }, \
+    { "AYA_HOME", 754 }, \
+    { "AYA_PERFORMANCE_CONSERVATION", 760 }, \
+    { "AYA_PERFORMANCE_BALANCE", 761 }, \
+    { "AYA_PREFORMANCE_MAX", 762 }
+
 // NOTE: If you add a new axis here you must also add it to several other files.
 //       Refer to frameworks/base/core/java/android/view/MotionEvent.java for the full list.
 #define AXES_SEQUENCE \
@@ -462,7 +475,7 @@
 // --- InputEventLookup ---
 
 InputEventLookup::InputEventLookup()
-      : KEYCODES({KEYCODES_SEQUENCE}),
+      : KEYCODES({KEYCODES_SEQUENCE, AYANEO_KEYCODES_SEQUENCE}),
         KEY_NAMES({KEYCODES_SEQUENCE}),
         AXES({AXES_SEQUENCE}),
         AXES_NAMES({AXES_SEQUENCE}),
